1
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:10,180
Goodbye, Haruta-kun.
Thank you for everything.

2
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,140
Launch!

3
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:15,960
I love Reiko. I have since long ago.

4
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:20,840
Don't get emotional.

5
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,520
Honda-san, you love shōjo manga, don't you?

6
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:27,180
Because she's the shōjo mangaka Otohime Nana,
after all.

7
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:31,720
Speaking of which, senpai, you're also serialized
in the same weekly magazine, Sapphire, aren't you?

8
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,620
Heh, this year marks my
third year of serialization.

9
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:41,940
I'm sure I had the manuscript for next week's issue.
Here it is.

10
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:46,340
I always fax them,
so the manuscripts stay on record.

11
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:48,340
Even so, there's no need to
throw them away, is there?

12
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:52,660
Senpai, your manga isn't in there.
I thought you'd quit.

13
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:55,680
What? I send my manuscripts
properly every week!

14
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,740
It's not even in the table of contents.

15
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:59,820
Not this one.

16
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,140
Reader's Square

17
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,060
They're treating you like an amateur

18
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:11,760
Come to think of it, you once turned my
12-page work into a 4-panel one, didn't you?

19
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,180
Are you properly discussing
things with your editor?

20
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:18,380
No, for the past few years there's been none at all.
The content and page count are up to me.

21
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,400
There's no such series, you know.

22
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:21,900
Manuscript fees...

23
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,200
I don't remember getting any lately.

24
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:29,040
Come to think of it,
the editorial department sent me a pendant.

25
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,960
Senpai, you mean this, right?

26
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,960
No, everyone got a present.

27
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,240
Looks like just a reader
who loves submitting.

28
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:39,520
Doesn't seem like a
serialized writer at all.

29
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:43,580
Ryusenshi, next time I see
him he won't get off so easy!

30
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:45,300
Hello.

31
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,400
Nana-chan.

32
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:48,900
Hello.

33
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,940
Honda-san, again?

34
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:55,140
I was really enjoying your
interesting stories, senpai.

35
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:58,120
Well, we have a date now, so

36
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:00,440
What, so I was just a way to kill time?

37
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:02,100
Well then, everyone.

38
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,560
Excuse us.

39
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,560
Oof, here we go.

40
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:06,800
Let's go!

41
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,780
Honda and Nana make such a perfect couple,
don't they?

42
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:14,900
They're so close. I'm really jealous.

43
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:18,920
Honda and Otohime,
the best couple everyone envies.

44
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:22,380
But little did anyone know that an outrageous
incident was about to befall these two.

45
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:25,260
No one could have known at that moment.

46
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:33,140
When you watch TV,
turn on the lights and sit back a bit, okay?

47
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:46,280
Anyone short on cash, come to me.

48
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:51,000
I've got none either, but don't worry.

49
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,840
Look at that blue sky.

50
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:58,340
White clouds.

51
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:04,700
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

52
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,000
You get it, right?

53
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,980
I get it, I get it.

54
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:13,920
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

55
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,220
The Great Love Sinking

56
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,100
Looks like we lost them.

57
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:44,480
They're still chasing us!

58
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,240
No way.

59
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:46,720
Stop, damn it!

60
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,720
He's a monster.

61
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,280
Pull over, I'm telling you!

62
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,860
I said stop!

63
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:02,260
You idiots! Did you really think you could
escape the great Honda of the late period?

64
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,623
Wait, the late-period Honda?

65
00:04:04,673 --> 00:04:07,600
You mean the legendary street racer Honda?

66
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,320
Sorry!

67
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,400
Sorry...

68
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,340
Did you catch up to him?

69
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,000
Yeah, totally got him.

70
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:26,020
Today's Super Footage scoop captures the moment
a reckless biker gang member was arrested.

71
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,560
Please take a look at
this thrilling footage.

72
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:39,180
This officer, who made a great catch, has the
nationwide number one arrest rate for traffic violators.

73
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,660
He's Officer Shun Honda of
the Katsushika Police Station.

74
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:43,440
Woohoo!

75
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,700
He got into the footage!

76
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,020
I saw you on TV.

77
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:52,840
You looked so cool on it.

78
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,120
Stop it, thanks, thanks,
you're making me blush.

79
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,840
Overnight,
you're the talk of the town, Honda.

80
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,040
Move over a little.

81
00:04:59,040 --> 00:04:59,780
You're in the way.

82
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:01,220
What? What?

83
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,080
Look at me

84
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:07,720
Honda, next time take
one with just me and you.

85
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,120
I'm first, too.

86
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,280
Me too.

87
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:13,140
Honda, you've really become popular.

88
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:14,800
Go on, keep at it.

89
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,220
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

90
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,320
Sen-

91
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:31,500
Senpai, look at this!

92
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:32,480
This.

93
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,380
W-what is this?

94
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:38,640
It's a pile of letters and
faxes addressed to Honda.

95
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:40,780
Emails to the Katsushika station too.

96
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:43,940
Apparently so many have come in,
the system's about to crash.

97
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:48,900
Even an active bōsōzoku sent a
helmet asking for his autograph.

98
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:52,540
Looks like you're a
bit of a modern-day hero.

99
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,720
Hero? No, I'm just -

100
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:59,540
This is Honda-kun's motorcycle.

101
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,120
I wonder if Honda-kun is here.

102
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,080
I'd love to get caught.

103
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:05,040
I want to ride behind Honda-kun.

104
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,720
I want to ride too.

105
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,560
Honda-kun...

106
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,780
It was Honda-kun.

107
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:13,060
What should we do, senpai?

108
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,740
If we go out now, it'll cause a panic.

109
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:17,440
Don't worry, it's fine.

110
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,420
Why is that?

111
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:22,120
That's right, the power of today's
high school girls is amazing.

112
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,360
If it's fine, then...

113
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:24,900
I mean, why?

114
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:29,760
Think about it. The public only knows
Honda's face from when he's riding his bike.

115
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,180
Now that you mention it...

116
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,000
Yeah, right.

117
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,400
*Stare*

118
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:34,900
Ugh.

119
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:44,340
See, the images don't match, right?

120
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:44,780
Yes.

121
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,880
So you can just go out
there with confidence.

122
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:48,580
Me!

123
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:50,660
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

124
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,520
Honda-kun, you!

125
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,720
The version when he's not on his bike.

126
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,600
Ugh!

127
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:59,760
Idiot! Senpai, help me! Senpai!

128
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:03,220
Damn, they've recognized
my everyday face too.

129
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:05,300
Help me, Senpai!

130
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,480
Guess I'll actually do some work for once.

131
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:10,120
Huh? I'll work too.

132
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,340
Please help me!

133
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:18,020
Wh-what's wrong, Honda!

134
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:21,580
S-senpai... I'm so down...

135
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,980
Did something happen?

136
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,400
Senpai!

137
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,100
Hey!

138
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,140
What's wrong?

139
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,440
Senpai, I'm finished.

140
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:35,520
I can't understand if you're just crying.
Explain it properly.

141
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,340
Here, Honda, a handkerchief.

142
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:39,220
Thank you very much.

143
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:41,660
Well, the thing is...

144
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:47,080
Ever since then, no matter where I go,
these fangirls keep stalking me.

145
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:51,026
Even when I'm eating,

146
00:07:51,076 --> 00:07:53,400
and last night, I couldn't calm down either.

147
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,140
Aaaaaah

148
00:07:58,140 --> 00:07:58,620
Aaaaaah

149
00:07:58,620 --> 00:07:59,640
Aaaaaah

150
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:11,160
So you had a fight with Otohime?

151
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,380
Yeah, that's right.

152
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,980
Even though we started
arguing over something trivial,

153
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:16,940
what should I do, senior?

154
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,780
Is that all?

155
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:20,960
"Is that all?" Ryo-chan, come on!

156
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:22,780
Yeah, that's right, senior!

157
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:23,380
Yes.

158
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:26,420
She's just jealous because
Honda suddenly became so popular.

159
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:29,520
Booms like this pass in no time at all.

160
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:31,020
Just hang in there until then.

161
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,580
You two will get back together, don't worry.

162
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,740
I can't stand it any longer.

163
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:38,020
Nana-chan won't even pick up my calls.

164
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:39,740
She won't even answer my emails.

165
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,480
I'm finished.

166
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,000
What a drama queen you are.

167
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,940
Don't come crying to me
over something like that.

168
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,240
Come on, go on home, go home.

169
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,820
Senior, it can't be that bad, right?

170
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:48,520
Shut up.

171
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:51,320
Sort out your own problems yourself.

172
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,700
Are you sure this is really okay, Ryo-san?

173
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,720
Time solves this kind of thing, you know.

174
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:00,860
Just leave them be.

175
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:04,200
I'm a master of romance,
so I'm telling you, there's no mistake.

176
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:07,220
Ryo-san, you're a master of romance?

177
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:09,360
I've never heard that before.

178
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,780
Well, a master of heartbreak, maybe.

179
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:12,480
Exactly.

180
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,620
Shut up!

181
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:15,960
Damn it, just watch.

182
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:20,780
Honda's absent from work?

183
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:24,560
He's been really serious lately.

184
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:28,460
Senior, is he really going to be okay?
Just leaving him like this?

185
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:32,780
It's fine. Trials like this will
make the couple's love stronger.

186
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,800
What he's saying makes sense, though.

187
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:38,620
Hello?

188
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,360
Dragon Warrior.

189
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:43,820
Hey! How dare you treat my
manga as if it didn't exist!

190
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,780
What, an emergency?

191
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:50,020
Otome's manuscript isn't finished?

192
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:54,680
That's right. Last time she missed the deadline too and we had to rescue her,
and this time it's dangerous as well.

193
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:58,240
Is this because of Honda's situation?

194
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:04,120
Yes. That's why I'm asking a favor: I want you,
Ryotsu, to smooth things over between the two of them.

195
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:06,760
So you want me to get them back together?

196
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:11,860
Otome's manga is our flagship title, and
another rescue would affect countless people.

197
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:16,320
If you cooperate,
I'll consider your serialization.

198
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,700
"I'll consider it" isn't the
right way to put it, is it?

199
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,380
You should say "please," shouldn't you?

200
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,400
Please.

201
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,280
Then I'll write the 50-page
Kanto Color feature for you,

202
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,780
so you'd better print it!

203
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:28,000
Well, that's a bit...

204
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:29,500
I see.

205
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,380
Understood.

206
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:34,520
We'll definitely print the
50-page Kanto Color feature.

207
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:35,480
Good.

208
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,760
I have a plan.

209
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,120
Just leave it to me and rest easy,
as if you're on a great ship.

210
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:40,500
Yes.

211
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:45,500
Yes.

212
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:49,020
A blind date for Honda?

213
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,520
Are you serious, senior?

214
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:53,160
Aren't we supposed to get
him back together with Nana?

215
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,080
It's shock therapy.

216
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,220
Shock therapy?

217
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:58,340
Will that really work?

218
00:10:58,580 --> 00:10:59,940
Leave it to me.

219
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:02,080
Honda-san.

220
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:03,740
Nana-chan.

221
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:11,220
The two gazing into each other's eyes
soon rush toward each other without a word.

222
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,360
Nana-chan! Hayato-san!

223
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:16,300
I'll never let you go,
not until the day I die.

224
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,980
I'm so happy, Hayato-san.

225
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:21,240
And the blind date
partner watching all this...

226
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:24,580
You two can't win against the power of love!

227
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:27,980
See? That's how it works.

228
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:30,800
Do you think it'll really go that well?

229
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:31,400
Yes.

230
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,240
Leave it to me.

231
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:37,580
After all, I'm a master of romance.

232
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:39,460
But who's going to play the other party?

233
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:41,100
The Chief, of course. The Chief!

234
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,380
Wake up, Honda!

235
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,780
Get up!

236
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:49,380
This is no time to be sleeping.
Get up already!

237
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:50,600
No thanks.

238
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:52,720
Just get up already.

239
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,360
Just leave me alone.

240
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,340
Otome isn't the only woman out there.

241
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,300
No, I only want Nana-chan.
I won't settle for anyone else.

242
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:00,520
Trust me, the romance expert.

243
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:04,160
I can only trust you three
times out of a thousand. Ugh.

244
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:06,180
Forget about the perks, anyway.

245
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,740
Go out and live your new life boldly.

246
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:09,940
This is bad.

247
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:16,000
Going by my past experience,
the blind dates the Chief recommends

248
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,340
are never any good, you know.

249
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:19,680
There's no way it'll work out,
even by mistake.

250
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,340
Honda, sorry to keep you waiting.

251
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:24,620
Thanks, Chief.

252
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,960
Come on in.

253
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:27,540
Yes.

254
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:30,880
W-wow, she's gorgeous!

255
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:33,040
I'm Norika from Asakusa.

256
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:46,820
Staying cooped up won't
give us any ideas, so

257
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:49,420
I'll treat you to a meal
today to clear your head.

258
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:49,880
Yes.

259
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:51,300
Well,

260
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:57,500
Well then, let's head out.

261
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:10,440
That's enough from the Chief. The rest
is up to you young ones. See you, Honda.

262
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:13,280
S-senpai!

263
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:18,620
Hehe, Honda-san, you have such cute eyes.

264
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:20,900
My eyes? My eyes?

265
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:24,860
I really love people with
gentle-looking eyes like yours.

266
00:13:25,410 --> 00:13:26,200
W-well...

267
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:30,820
I have every magazine you've been featured in,
Honda-san.

268
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,640
R-really?

269
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:36,971
I've even recorded everything
you've been on TV on video,

270
00:13:37,021 --> 00:13:40,060
but the real you is even
nicer than on TV or in photos.

271
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:42,740
Hi there!

272
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,740
Ahahaha!

273
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,060
Mr. Honda, am I your type?

274
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:48,240
What do you think?

275
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:49,900
Hey,

276
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,740
I-I mean, you're that beautiful.

277
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:55,780
Not that, but do you like me or not?

278
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,000
Come on,

279
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:57,780
which is it?

280
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:00,220
Do you like composing music?

281
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:04,140
I forgot something.

282
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:04,900
What is it?

283
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:06,660
You're hopeless, you know that?

284
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,960
I'll just go grab it.

285
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:11,040
Chief, please go on ahead. See you.

286
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:17,820
This food looks delicious!
Come on, eat up and cheer up!

287
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:18,940
Yeah.

288
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,140
Hey, Taro.

289
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:25,560
Yes.

290
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:27,620
She's just too cute.

291
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:31,880
This should be the spot
where Ryusen-shi and Otome are.

292
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,500
Well then.

293
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,440
There they are, there they are.

294
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:44,120
With this remote-control
mouse I prepared earlier.

295
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:46,160
Go!

296
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:52,860
M-mouse!

297
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,840
Not mice! Anything but mice!

298
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,820
Damn, wrong target!

299
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,560
Move properly!

300
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:09,540
Ryusen-san

301
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:13,680
Nana-chan

302
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,340
Nana-chan

303
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:19,680
What's wrong with it?

304
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,960
Nana-chan

305
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:27,120
Nana-chan

306
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:31,500
See? Perfect, right?
It's a little different from the plan, but

307
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,800
You set this up, didn't you, senpai?

308
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:37,120
Ryo-san, this isn't what you promised!

309
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:38,700
Is that so?

310
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,600
That's terrible, senpai.

311
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:45,660
Nana-chan completely hates me now, you know!

312
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,440
At this rate,
I'd be better off dead, seriously.

313
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:57,280
Well, at the other day's omiai, the
other side really took a liking to Honda.

314
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:00,500
They said they want to date
him with marriage in mind.

315
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,300
They're asking if tomorrow would work.

316
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:05,281
Hey, Ryotsu,

317
00:16:05,331 --> 00:16:08,720
could you find a date
course for the two of them?

318
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,080
Yeah, yeah.

319
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:11,900
Well, I'm counting on you.

320
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:14,900
Thanks to my masterful matchmaking,
we've got our first couple!

321
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,800
What are we going to do, Ryo-chan?

322
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:18,600
That's right, senpai.

323
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:21,020
Well, there was a bit of a mix-up.

324
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:24,720
At this rate,
those two are going to be over for good.

325
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:28,460
Romance expert, my foot.

326
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:29,840
This is all your fault, Ryo-chan.

327
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:30,600
I know.

328
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,580
But surely there's some clever way...

329
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:40,580
No matter how many times I watch it,
this movie always makes me cry.

330
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,080
Yes, that's it!

331
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:47,320
We'll bring Honda and Otohime
together in an extreme situation.

332
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:49,200
This is the only way.

333
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:56,260
Nana-chan, I don't care what happens to me.

334
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:58,540
You have to live on for both of us.

335
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:00,140
No way, no, no.

336
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:06,020
We can't compete with
the strength of your love.

337
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:10,000
Be happy, both of you, for me too.

338
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,580
And when they see the two of them bound together by love,
so tightly, so firmly,

339
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:15,540
the other side will give up too.

340
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:19,480
Nakagawa, Nakagawa, at Amusement C...

341
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,760
Build me a good attraction.

342
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:23,500
We'll do it during the
special construction work.

343
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,960
Hurry up, we have to finish it by tomorrow.

344
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:44,960
And then...

345
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:51,340
Senpai, I don't want anyone but Nana-chan.

346
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,440
It's the Chief's orders.

347
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,360
This way.

348
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,460
Senpai.

349
00:17:58,020 --> 00:17:59,600
Hurry up and follow me.

350
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:01,360
Y-yes.

351
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:04,080
This way.

352
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:07,080
I'm not in the mood to
come to a place like this.

353
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,620
Come on, it's fine, it's fine.

354
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:11,780
Nothing beats having fun and forgetting your troubles,
you know.

355
00:18:11,780 --> 00:18:12,820
That's right.

356
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:14,500
This one's good, isn't it?

357
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:15,320
But...

358
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,240
Wow, that looks fun.

359
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,600
Let's cheer up.

360
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:19,180
Yes.

361
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:22,360
This is the place, right?

362
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,500
You're Norika from Asakusa, right?

363
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:26,800
Yes.

364
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,520
Mr. Honda says he'll be a little late.

365
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:33,240
I was told to keep you company until then.

366
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:37,460
There's a tearoom over there,
so let's wait there.

367
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:38,180
Yes.

368
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:45,680
Alright, this is where it starts.

369
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:48,940
Weren't you supposed to be
going on a date with Norika?

370
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:49,540
That's right.

371
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,140
Excuse me.

372
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:04,620
These are all robots, you know, robots!

373
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:10,020
Wow! Look, look, that outfit is so cute!

374
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:19,380
Nakagawa-san, that one inside is the Contel emer...
I have every magazine you've been in.

375
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:20,860
S-so is that right?

376
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:27,980
Aaaah! Senpai, that just now...

377
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:31,160
We've collided with an iceberg.
Everyone, please evacuate.

378
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:32,980
Iceberg.

379
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:45,640
Right, next, just Honda and Otohime,
the two of them alone.

380
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,180
Nana-chan.

381
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:54,300
Honda-san.

382
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:56,160
Aaaaah!

383
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:58,200
Hey, aren't you an old man!

384
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,160
What do you think you're doing!

385
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,220
Hey, stop talking!

386
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:02,720
Nana-chan...

387
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:04,100
Honda-san...

388
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:25,080
Why is a caveman

389
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:29,780
the damn computer got it wrong?

390
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:30,700
Seriously.

391
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,160
Let go of me!

392
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:40,960
What is it?

393
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:43,560
The ship's going to split in two and sink!

394
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:46,060
Damn it!

395
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,200
Kogachi, grab onto this!

396
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:55,120
Damn you!

397
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:03,160
It's sinking!

398
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:10,940
Eeeeeeeh!

399
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:14,200
Eeeeeeeh!

400
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:17,620
Eeeeeeeh!

401
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:17,940
Eeeeeeeh!

402
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,420
Eeeeeeeh!

403
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:20,480
Eeeeeeeh!

404
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:20,540
Eeeeeeeh!

405
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:20,600
Eeeeeeeh!

406
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:21,760
Eeeeeeeh!

407
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:23,360
Eeeeeeeh!

408
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:27,680
Move over more, would you?

409
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:29,800
You're the one who should
stop sticking to me!

410
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:30,580
No way.

411
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:31,800
I'm the one who should be saying that!

412
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:32,560
Move!

413
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:33,480
Don't come near me!

414
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:38,760
Hey, this is the same as the Titanic, right?

415
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:42,220
Then after this,
only you will sink, glub glub, right?

416
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:43,780
Don't get too cocky!

417
00:21:43,780 --> 00:21:47,780
But no, if it's exactly the same,
it wouldn't be any fun.

418
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:51,160
Wait, what's with this music?

419
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,380
Idiot! Why of all things a shark?

420
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,414
The more desperate things get,

421
00:21:57,464 --> 00:22:00,020
the more our hearts will bond tightly,
or so they say.

422
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:01,480
Ow ow!

423
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:05,060
I'd rather be eaten by a
shark than bond with you!

424
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:06,140
Me too!

425
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:11,440
Then you be the one who gets eaten!

426
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:12,640
You first!

427
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:14,560
That's right, keep going, fight back!

428
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:15,480
Shut up!

429
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,120
Grab onto that ball!

430
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:24,660
What is this? What's going on?

431
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:31,940
I'm not spending eternity in
love with this caveman, no way!

432
00:22:31,940 --> 00:22:34,940
I don't want to be stuck
with this Jajanma either!

433
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:36,100
Don't touch me!

434
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:47,200
Ryo-chan, well done!

435
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,160
Where are Honda and Otome?

436
00:22:52,060 --> 00:22:53,360
Over there!

437
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:56,407
Just as Ryo-chan said,

438
00:22:56,457 --> 00:22:58,880
this extreme situation
has revived their love.

439
00:22:59,380 --> 00:23:01,800
As expected, you're a master of romance.

440
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,020
But...

441
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:07,160
What master? Hmph!

442
00:23:07,180 --> 00:23:09,200
W-what, you Jajanmaa!

443
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:10,760
You caveman!

444
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:11,820
Maybe it'll actually work!

445
00:23:11,820 --> 00:23:13,720
Looks like some couples aren't like that.

446
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:16,180
Help me, senpai!

447
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:18,340
Nakagawa-san

448
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:19,900
What is it, Nakagawa?

449
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:23,400
She says she likes me better than Honda-san!

450
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,540
Wait, Keichi-san!

451
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:28,100
Nana-chan

452
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:29,180
Honda-san

453
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:36,480
No, no, no.

454
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,240
What's wrong?

455
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:39,020
Senpai.

456
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:42,800
We promised Ryu a 50-page feature,
all in color, didn't we?

457
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,400
It's not printed anywhere!

458
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:46,520
This one, right?

459
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:51,920
It looks like a fingerprint,
but look closer, it's a row of swirls.

460
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:54,640
It's definitely on the gravure page.

461
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:57,000
It's printed in full color on every page.

462
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,880
Ryo-chan, you got one over on you.

463
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,640
Damn it! Remember this!

464
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:03,620
Next time, you won't get off so easy!

465
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:24,420
To the guys who go all-in
on reckless gambling at Luxus

466
00:24:24,420 --> 00:24:27,400
I probably don't want to become that

467
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:32,000
if you're dawdling at the street corner

468
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,300
the moon has run away

469
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:37,900
because now isn't everything

470
00:24:38,740 --> 00:24:42,540
Don't get too worked up about it

471
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:46,280
even if you fudge the truth a little

472
00:24:46,280 --> 00:24:50,440
once in a while, when you're helping someone

473
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:53,450
Baby, do you know me?

474
00:24:53,500 --> 00:24:54,520
Toward tomorrow

475
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:56,760
A nice spirit

476
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:01,800
Don't lose heart, I'll do what needs doing

477
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:04,260
A cute spirit

478
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:07,660
What's hard to understand

479
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:11,120
is wanting to look that way

480
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:17,360
Better than a facade, right?

481
00:25:30,660 --> 00:25:32,440
Here comes the World Cup!

482
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:35,340
A soccer tournament to
win that platinum ticket!

483
00:25:35,340 --> 00:25:37,040
We're definitely getting it!

484
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:40,860
What? The soccer field is double-booked,
so the match can't be played?

485
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:44,301
It's Akagawa Stadium! Next time,

486
00:25:44,351 --> 00:25:47,220
Machikado Soccer 2002! See you then!

487
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:50,880
That place is Kameari.

488
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:54,800
Well, it's definitely Kameari.

489
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:57,275
Everyone, come on over,

490
00:25:57,325 --> 00:25:59,220
to our town!

491
00:26:00,380 --> 00:26:00,820
Thank you!

